6. Full Misconception Specification
6.1 Misconception Schema
The misconception schema defines the structure of a misconception deposit.

It has the following fields:

misconception_id. A string. Required.

misconception_name. A string. Required.

description. A string. Required.

subject. A string. Required.

topic. A string. Required.

age_range. An object. Required. It contains min_age and max_age.

persistence. An enum. The values are low, medium, high, very_high.

root_cause. A string. Optional.

evidence_for. An array of evidence objects. Required.

evidence_against. An array of evidence objects. Optional.

interventions_that_work. An array of intervention objects. Optional.

interventions_that_fail. An array of intervention objects. Optional.

related_misconceptions. An array of misconception relations. Optional.

provenance. An object. Required.

stag_annotation. An object. Optional.

work_reference. A string. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

Each evidence object has:

evidence_id. A string.

study_reference. A string.

study_summary. A string.

sample_size. An integer.

age_range. An object. It contains min_age and max_age.

observation. A string.

statistical_result. A string.

Each intervention object has:

intervention_id. A string.

intervention_name. A string.

intervention_description. A string.

intervention_type. An enum. The values are direct_instruction, inquiry_based, peer_instruction, demonstration, simulation, hands_on, other.

study_reference. A string.

result. An object. It contains outcome, effect_size, and statistical_significance.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each misconception relation has:

relation_id. A string.

related_misconception_id. A string.

relation_type. An enum. The values are same_root_cause, prerequisite, related, independent.

relation_note. A string. Optional.

