7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Misconception
function createMisconception(misconception, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the misconception against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the STAG annotation is present, validate it.

Step 4. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. Generate a misconception ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 6. Insert the misconception.

Step 7. Insert the evidence records, the intervention records, and the relation records.

Step 8. Insert the STAG link and the work link if present.

Step 9. Insert the provenance.

Step 10. Insert the moderation record.

Step 11. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 12. Return the misconception_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Misconception
function readMisconception(misconceptionId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the misconception. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the evidence, the interventions, the relations, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Misconception
function updateMisconception(misconceptionId, misconception, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing misconception. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new misconception.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the misconception_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Misconception
function deleteMisconception(misconceptionId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing misconception. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the misconception_id and the status deleted.

7.5 Query Misconceptions
function queryMisconceptions(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the query.

Step 3. Read the matching misconceptions.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the misconceptions, the count, and the pagination.

7.6 Aggregate Misconceptions
function aggregateMisconceptions(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the aggregation.

Step 3. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 4. Return the results.

7.7 Full-Text Search
function fullTextSearch(query, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Build and execute the search.

Step 3. Read the matching misconceptions.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the misconceptions and the count.

7.8 Export Misconception
function exportMisconception(misconceptionId, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the deposit.

Step 3. If json, output the deposit. If provo, export to PROV-O. If turtle, serialize to Turtle.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the format.

7.9 Bulk Import
function bulkImport(file, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Parse the file.

Step 3. For each misconception, call createMisconception.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the results and the count.

7.10 Bulk Export
function bulkExport(query, format, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the matching misconceptions.

Step 3. If json, output the list. If jsonl, output one line per misconception. If provo, export each one.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the output and the count.

7.11 Moderate Misconception
function moderateMisconception(misconceptionId, moderationStatus, moderationNotes, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "moderator"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing misconception. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Update the moderation status. Insert a moderation record.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the misconception_id and the status.

7.12 Misconception Map
function misconceptionMap(auth, options):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read all misconceptions.

Step 3. Build the map with subjects as axes and root causes as positions.

Step 4. Return the map.

7.13 Intervention Comparison View
function interventionComparisonView(misconceptionId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the misconception. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the interventions that work and the interventions that fail.

Step 4. Build the comparison by overlaying the effect sizes.

Step 5. Return the comparison.

7.14 Persistence Curve
